Known non-deterministic corruption in the ARM64 build of z3-4.3.1: the
response to this test's check-sat command is truncated well short of
where the real output should end and replaced with spurious "unexpected
character" parse errors whose exact text (line/column, repetition count)
differs from run to run against the identical binary -- confirmed by
comparing CI captures across the sibling ok_checkQuantifiedTrans* and
ok_forallBoolUnSat tests in the same run. A .bad golden (exact-match) can
never stay in sync with genuinely non-deterministic output, so this is
skipped rather than pinned to one observed variant. Never seen on x64.
See https://github.com/smtlib/jSMTLIB/issues/101 for the broader ARM64
z3-4.3.1 correctness-bug tracking issue.
